# Reference material, deliberately not deployed.
#
# assets/reference/ holds the source photographs the monuments are built FROM —
# 922 Commons images of the Shore Temple, plus the photogrammetry working set
# with full-resolution originals. Several gigabytes. Nothing in the site loads
# any of it (js/wiki-photo.js fetches its photographs from Wikipedia at runtime),
# so shipping it would mean uploading gigabytes on every deploy to serve nothing.
#
# There is a licensing reason too. Most of these are CC BY-SA: publishing them
# from this domain would be redistribution, and redistribution carries the
# attribution condition. The credits exist — assets/reference/*/SOURCES.md — but
# they are not rendered anywhere on the site, so the honest position is not to
# serve the images at all until they are.
assets/reference/

# Local build caches for the fetch scripts. Regenerated on demand.
scripts/.shore-temple-cache.json
scripts/.shore-temple-survey.json

# The uncompressed original of the monument GLB. Kept in the repo because any
# re-export must start from it (recompressing already-quantized data stacks the
# error), but it is 1.6 MB and nothing loads it at runtime.
assets/models/mamallapuram-monuments.glb.bak

# Two three.js r185 minified files that nothing imports. The live build is the
# r169 assets/vendor/three.module.js (which is itself minified); these two were
# measured at 188 KB gzipped TOGETHER against 170 KB for the file in use, so
# "switching to the min build" would be larger, not smaller, and would need the
# addons' './three.module.js' specifiers rewritten. Kept for reference, not shipped.
assets/vendor/three.module.min.js
assets/vendor/three.core.min.js

# Never loaded at runtime: the superseded penance base GLB (302 KB gz) and a
# 1.4 MB render preview of the Shore Temple model.
assets/models/arjunas-penance-base.glb
assets/models/shore-temple-preview.png

# The uncompressed Shore Temple export (JPEG textures, no vertex normals) that
# meshopt compression starts from. Kept for the same reason as the monuments
# .bak — never recompress an already-quantized file — and never served.
assets/models/shore-temple.glb.bak
assets/models/pancha-rathas.glb.bak
